 "insight": [
  "Luxembourg's total trade index reached 123 in 2025, the lowest among the eight countries compared, with Belgium, the Netherlands, Germany, France, Austria, Spain, and Italy all having higher indices.",
  "The Netherlands had the highest trade index at 266 in 2025, followed by Spain at 221 and Germany at 208.",
  "Luxembourg was the only country where the intra-EU share of trade increased, rising by 5.0 percentage points to 85.2%, while all other countries saw declines.",
  "Luxembourg's total trade value in 2025 was 41.35 billion euros, much smaller than Germany's 2,925.24 billion euros and the Netherlands' 1,648.33 billion euros.",
  "The data are presented in current euros and are not adjusted for price changes, which may affect comparisons over time."
 ],
